---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import icon from '@assets/logo.svg';
import icon_name from '@assets/logo_name.svg';
import LineBreak from "@components/LineBreak.astro";
---

<header>
	<div class="menu">
		<a id="a-intro">About</a>
		<a id="a-practical-information">Submission Guidelines</a>
		<!--<a id="a-program">Program</a>-->
		<a id="a-sponsors">Organizers</a>
	</div>
	<div><a class="icon" id="a-title" style="padding: 0"><Image src={icon_name} alt="XRTransitions"/></a></div>
	<div class="menu">
	</div>
</header>
<div id="container">
	<section id="title">
		<Image src={icon} alt="RJC IHM 2026" class="rjc-logo"/>
		<h1>Collaborative XRTransitions</h1>
		<h2>The First International Workshop on the Multiple Dimensions of the Transitions in Collaborative eXtended Reality</h2>
		<h3>In conjunction with the 25th IEEE International Symposium on Mixed and Augmented Reality (ISMAR 2026)</h3>
		<p style="text-align: center;">6th October 2026</p>
	</section>
	<LineBreak/>

	<section id="intro">
		<h3>Venue</h3>
		<p>The workshop will be held physically in Bari, Italy.</p>
	</section>
	<LineBreak/>


	<section id="intro">
		<h3>Themes of the workshop</h3>
			<p>
				<strong>The XRTransitions ISMAR workshop aims to explore the multiple dimensions of the transitions between collaborative situations in extended reality</strong>. We will first examine whether transitions in single-user cross-reality systems apply to collaborative situations or need to be adapted for them. Then, other dimensions specific to collaborative situations will be explored, going beyond what has already been studied in single-user cross-reality systems. These include control over the transition—who initiates it, who executes it, and who stops it—as well as the awareness of other collaborators regarding transitions performed by a user.
			</p>
		<br>
		<p>
			<em>Rationale</em>: The number of collaborative systems in extended reality scenarios has considerably increased these last years, using shared spaces, tasks or objects that blur the boundaries between physical and digital life. Nowadays, collaborative XR environments have many applications, for example in the fields of education, training, industrial manufacturing, design, architecture, and urban planning. These applications define varied, often dynamic, collaborative situations. Multiple dimensions of collaborative situations have been explored depending on the number of users involved, the nature of the tasks to be performed, the manipulated objects, and the characteristics of the environment.
			In the meanwhile, collaborative XR environments often require users to adapt to changing tasks, roles, spatial arrangements, interaction modalities, and levels of immersion. Designing efficient transitions between these collaborative situations is therefore essential for maintaining users’ awareness, coordination, communication, and overall engagement. However, the definition of seamless and efficient transitions between collaborative situations still remains underexplored. Indeed, while transitions and transitional interfaces are key concepts in the study of single-user cross-reality systems (see the scoping survey on Cross-reality Systems by Auda et al. <a href="https://doi.org/10.1145/3616536">https://doi.org/10.1145/3616536</a>), the design of transitions within collaborative situations has not been studied in a systematic manner. A better understanding of such transitions could improve the continuity, usability, and effectiveness of collaborative XR experiences across a wide range of applications.
		</p>
		</section>

		<section id="topics">
			<h3>Topics of Interest</h3>
			<p>This workshop aims to bring together researchers and practitioners interested in transitions in single-user or collaborative cross-reality systems, fostering discussions on interaction techniques, user experience, system design, and applications that enable efficient transitions along the continuum from physical to virtual environments. Topics of interest include:</p>
		<ul style="margin-top:0; padding-top:0;">
				<li>
					Case studies of collaborative extended reality systems;
				</li>
				<li>
					Examples of transitional interfaces in single-user or collaborative cross-reality systems;
				</li>
				<li>
					Characterization of the dimensions of transitional interfaces in single-user or collaborative cross-reality systems.
				</li>
			</ul>
	</section>

	<section id="practical-information">
		<h3>Submission Guidelines</h3>
		<div id="dates">
			<ul>
				<li>Submission deadline: July 05th, 2026</li>
				<li>Notification deadline: July 17th, 2026</li>
				<li>Camera-ready deadline: July 31st, 2026</li>
				<li>Workshop: 8 October 2026 (tentative depending on conference limitations)</li>
			</ul>
		</div>

		<p style="position:relative; top:-5px;">All deadlines are 23:59 AoE.</p>

		<br>
		<p>We welcome paper submissions of <strong>4–6 pages</strong>, excluding references and appendices. Examples of submissions include:</p>
		<ul style="margin-top:0; padding-top:0;">
			<li><strong>Case study papers:</strong> Papers describing case studies of collaborative cross-reality systems.</li>
			<li><strong>Position papers:</strong> Original research with preliminary results addressing transitions in single-user or collaborative cross-reality systems.</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Short survey papers:</strong> Review papers presenting a set of dimensions that characterize transitions in single-user or collaborative cross-reality systems.
			</li>
		</ul>

		<p>Submissions should be anonymous and follow the VGTC conference template, see <a href="https://tc.computer.org/vgtc/publications/conference/">https://tc.computer.org/vgtc/publications/conference/</a>. Papers must be submitted through the EasyChair system. Each submission will be reviewed by at least two program committee members following a single-blind review process. Accepted papers will be published in the IEEE Digital Library within the IEEE ISMAR Abstract and Workshop proceedings. At least one author of each accepted paper is required to register, attend, and present their work at XRTransitions.</p>
		<br>
		<p>
		We also allow submissions without publication. For these, authors may submit a <strong>2-page abstract</strong>, following the same template as the papers.
		</p>

	</section>

	<LineBreak/>
	<section id="organizers">
		<h3>Organizers</h3>
		<h4>General Chairs</h4>
		<ul>
			<li>
				<a href=" https://adrienchaffangeon.xyz/">Adrien Chaffangeon Caillet</a> (University Grenoble Alpes, France)
			</li>
			<li>
				<a href="https://people.irisa.fr/Maud.Marchal/">Maud Marchal</a> (Univ. Rennes, INSA, IRISA, France)
			</li>
			<li>
				<a href=" https://iihm.imag.fr/nigay/">Laurence Nigay</a> (University Grenoble Alpes, France)
			</li>
		</ul>

		<h4>Program Committee</h4>
		<ul>
			<li>Mark Billinghurst (University of South Australia, Australia)</li>
			<li>Gerd Bruder (University of Central Florida, USA)</li>
			<li>Jean-Marie Burkhardt (University Gustave Eiffel, France)</li>
			<li>Christian Sandor (Université Paris-Saclay, France)</li>
			<li>Marcos Serrano (University of Toulouse, France)</li>
		</ul>

	</section>

	<LineBreak/>
	<section id="contact">
		<h3>Contact Information</h3>
		All questions about submissions should be emailed to the chairs: <a href="mailto:xrtransitions@gmail.com">xrtransitions@gmail.com</a>
	</section>

	<LineBreak/>
	<section id="acks">
		<h3>Acknowledgements</h3>
		This workshop is supported by the French national research program <a href="https://www.pepr-ensemble.fr/en/">eNSEMBLE</a>, funded by France 2030, which brings together scientists from multiple disciplines to address current challenges in digital collaboration.
	</section>

	<section id="footer"></section>
</div>

<script>
	function changeCss () {
		let headerElement = document.querySelector("header");
		if (headerElement === null) return
		window.scrollY > 10 ? headerElement.classList.add("shadow") : headerElement.classList.remove("shadow")
	}
	window.addEventListener("scroll", changeCss , false);

	function scrollToId (name: string) {
		let element = document.getElementById(name);
		if (element === null) return
		element.scrollIntoView({
			behavior: 'smooth', // smooth scrolling
			block: 'start'      // align to top
		});
		// window.scrollTo(
		// 	{
		// 		top: Math.max(0, element.getBoundingClientRect().top-80),
		// 		left: 0,
		// 		behavior: "smooth",
		// 	})
	}
	document.getElementById("a-intro")
		?.addEventListener("click", () => scrollToId("intro"))
	document.getElementById("a-practical-information")
		?.addEventListener("click", () => scrollToId("practical-information"))
	document.getElementById("a-program")
		?.addEventListener("click", () => scrollToId("program"))
	document.getElementById("a-sponsors")
		?.addEventListener("click", () => scrollToId("organizers"))
	document.getElementById("a-title")
		?.addEventListener("click", () => scrollToId("title"))
	document.getElementById("a-application-process")
		?.addEventListener("click", () => scrollToId("application-process"))

</script>

<style>
	#container {
		font-family: Inter, Roboto, 'Helvetica Neue', 'Arial Nova', 'Nimbus Sans', Arial, sans-serif;
		min-height: 100%;
		max-width: 1200px;
		margin: auto;
		padding-left: 50px;
		padding-right: 50px;
		padding-bottom: 150px;
	}

	section {
		scroll-margin-top: 85px; /* height of sticky header */
	}

	main {
		height: 100%;
		display: flex;
		justify-content: center;
	}

	h1 {
		font-size: 2em;
		margin-top: 0.25em;
		margin-bottom: 0.25em;
	}

	header {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 45% 10% 45%;
		padding: 20px 60px;
		background: white;
		font-family: Inter, Roboto, 'Helvetica Neue', 'Arial Nova', 'Nimbus Sans', Arial, sans-serif;
		position: sticky;
		top: 0;
		transition: 0.5s;
	}

	header.shadow {
		box-shadow: rgba(60, 64, 67, 0.3) 0px 1px 2px 0px, rgba(60, 64, 67, 0.15) 0px 1px 3px 1px;
		transition: 0.5s;
	}

	header div:nth-child(2) {
		justify-self: center;
	}

	header div:nth-child(3) {
		justify-self: end;
	}

	header img {
		width: 200px;
		height: auto;
	}

	#title{
		text-align: center;
		margin-top: 10px;
		margin-bottom: 20px;
	}

	#title h1 {
		margin-bottom: 0;
	}

	#title h3 {
		margin-top: 0;
		font-weight: normal;
		font-size: smaller;
		color: gray;
	}

	#dates ul, #organizers ul {
		margin-left: 0;
		margin-top: 7px;
		padding-left: 0;
		list-style-type: none;
	}

	#links, #sponsor-logo-container {
		display: flex;
		gap: 16px;
		width: 90%;
		margin: 0 auto;
	}

	img.sponsor-logo {
		height: 50px;
		width: auto;
		margin: 0 25px;
	}

	header a {
		display: inline-flex;
		align-items: center;
		padding: 10px 12px;
		color: #1f1f1f;
		text-decoration: none;
		transition: color 0.2s;
	}

	header a:hover {
		color: #e86d15;
		font-weight: bolder;
	}

	header a svg {
		height: 1em;
		margin-left: 8px;
	}

	a.button {
		color: white;
		/*background: linear-gradient(160deg, #f3bb54 0%,#c55ca3 50%, #5a62ac 100%);*/
		background: #f3bb54;
		box-shadow:
			inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12),
			inset 0 -2px 0 rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.24);
		border-radius: 10px;
	}

	a.button:hover, header a.button:hover {
		transition: 600ms;
		color: #000000;
		font-weight: normal;
		box-shadow: none;
	}

	a.icon {
		font-weight: bold;
		font-size: large;
	}

	pre {
		font-family:
			ui-monospace, 'Cascadia Code', 'Source Code Pro', Menlo, Consolas, 'DejaVu Sans Mono',
			monospace;
		font-weight: normal;
		background: linear-gradient(14deg, #d83333 0%, #f041ff 100%);
		-webkit-background-clip: text;
		-webkit-text-fill-color: transparent;
		background-clip: text;
		margin: 0;
	}

	h2 {
		margin: 0;
		font-weight: normal;
		color: #111827;
		font-size: 20px;
	}

	h3 {
		margin-top: 10px;
		margin-bottom: 5px;
		font-weight: initial;
		font-size: 2em;
		color: #343333;
	}

	h4 {
		margin-top: 20px;
		margin-bottom: 5px;
		font-weight: initial;
		font-size: 1.5em;
		color: #343333;
	}


	p {
		color: #4b5563;
		font-size: 16px;
		line-height: 24px;
		letter-spacing: -0.006em;
		margin: 0;
		text-align: justify;
	}

	code {
		display: inline-block;
		background:
			linear-gradient(66.77deg, #f3cddd 0%, #f5cee7 100%) padding-box,
			linear-gradient(155deg, #d83333 0%, #f041ff 18%, #f5cee7 45%) border-box;
		border-radius: 8px;
		border: 1px solid transparent;
		padding: 6px 8px;
	}

	.box {
		padding: 16px;
		background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1);
		border-radius: 16px;
		border: 1px solid white;
	}

	.rjc-logo {
		max-width: 80%;
	}

	#program-container {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 110px repeat(5, auto);
	}

	#program-container .classe {
		background: rgb(138 215 245);
	}

	#program-container .break {
		background: rgb(245 231 138);
	}

	#program-container .workshop {
		background: rgb(139 214 90);
	}

	#program-container .other {
		background: rgb(245 138 165);
	}

	#program-container .activity {
		background: rgb(241 138 245);
	}

	#program-container .orga {
		background: rgb(222 222 222);
	}

	#program-container div div {
		border-top: 1px solid lightgray;
		border-left: 1px solid lightgray;
		padding: 5px;
	}

	#program-container #program-friday div {
		border-right: 1px solid lightgray;
	}

	#program-container div div:nth-child(1) {
		height: 20px;
	}

	#program-container div div:nth-child(2) {
		height: 20px;
	}

	#program-container div div:nth-child(3) {
		height: 60px;
	}

	#program-container div div:nth-child(4) {
		height: 20px;
	}

	#program-container div div:nth-child(5) {
		height: 60px;
	}

	#program-container div div:nth-child(6) {
		height: 20px;
	}

	#program-container div div:nth-child(7) {
		height: 80px;
	}

	#program-container div div:nth-child(8) {
		height: 60px;
	}

	#program-container div div:nth-child(9) {
		height: 20px;
	}

	#program-container div div:nth-child(10) {
		height: 60px;
	}

	#program-container div div:nth-child(11) {
		height: 20px;
	}

	#program-container div div:nth-child(12) {
		height: 40px;
	}

	#program-container div div:nth-child(13) {
		height: 20px;
		border-bottom: 1px solid lightgray;
	}

	.mobile-time {
		display: none;
	}

	#footer {
		height: 200px;
	}

	@media screen and (max-width: 784px) {
		header {
			grid-template-columns: 100%;
			padding: 20px 30px;
		}

		header div:nth-child(2) {
			justify-self: center;
			text-align: center;
		}
		.menu {
			display: none;
		}
	}

	@media screen and (max-width: 900px) {
		#container, #program-container {
			display: flex;
			flex-direction: column;
		}

		#container {
			padding: 20px;
		}

		#program-container #program-time, #program-container .empty {
			display: none;
		}

		.mobile-time {
			display: initial;
			font-weight: bold;
		}

		#program-container > div {
			margin-bottom: 10px;
		}

		#program-container div div {
			max-width: 400px;
			height: auto;
			margin: auto;
		}

		 a.button {
			padding: 14px 18px;
		}

		h1 {
			line-height: 1.5;
		}
	}
</style>
